# The demo runs with `npm run dev` and no configuration at all.
# A production start needs AUTH_SECRET, and sign-in needs an email provider.

# Signs session cookies. Required in production — without it the app refuses
# to sign anyone in rather than falling back to a key published in the source.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# AUTH_SECRET=

# Storage. Unset, the app uses a JSON file at data/db.json — zero setup, and
# single-process only, so it is for local work and demos rather than traffic.
# Set this and it uses Postgres; run `npm run migrate` before starting.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/blindbox

# Who can administer the shop. A comma-separated list of email addresses; those
# accounts get admin the next time they sign in. Unset, the console is open in
# development and refuses to load in production — an unprotected inventory
# editor should never be the accidental default.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=you@yourdomain.com,partner@yourdomain.com

# When you replace the mock payment provider in src/lib/payments.ts with a real
# one, its keys belong here — for Stripe, that is the pair below.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Sign in with Apple — the way people sign up. All four must be set together;
# with any of them missing the app falls back to the emailed-link flow, which
# outside development refuses rather than quietly offering a second door.
#
# Getting them means a paid Apple Developer account:
#   APPLE_CLIENT_ID   the Services ID (e.g. app.bricks.web), NOT the App ID
#   APPLE_TEAM_ID     the ten-character team id, top right of the portal
#   APPLE_KEY_ID      the ten-character id of the Sign in with Apple key
#   APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY the whole .p8 file, BEGIN/END lines included
#
# Apple will not accept localhost as a Return URL, so this cannot be exercised
# on a development machine — that is what the fallback is for.
# APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=
# APPLE_KEY_ID=
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
#
# Only needed when the app cannot work out its own public URL — behind a proxy
# the request's origin can be an internal hostname, and this has to match a
# registered Return URL character for character.
# APPLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-domain/auth/apple/callback

# Sign-in emails. Both must be set together, or nothing is sent and sign-in
# refuses in production. EMAIL_FROM must be on a domain verified with Resend,
# or Resend rejects the message.
#
# Still here because ADMIN_EMAILS grants the console by address, and somebody
# signing in with Hide My Email arrives as a relay that will not match it.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# EMAIL_FROM=Blind Box <hello@yourdomain.com>
